window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0d7ccc9567143e24"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-for-ios\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"ios\">为 iOS 构建应用</h1> <p>使用 Codex 为 iPhone 和 iPad 搭建、构建并调试 SwiftUI 应用。</p> <p>使用 Codex 搭建 iOS SwiftUI 项目，以 <code>xcodebuild</code> 或 Tuist 为先构建命令行循环；当工作更深入时，再加入 XcodeBuildMCP 或有针对性的 SwiftUI 技能。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>希望 Codex 从零搭建应用和构建循环的全新 iOS SwiftUI 项目。</li> <li>在完成工作前，需要 Codex 检查 scheme、模拟器输出、截图或自动化界面的现有 iPhone 与 iPad 项目。</li> <li>希望长期运行的 iOS 界面任务继续以代理方式和命令行为先，而不是依赖 Xcode 图形界面的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>构建或重构 SwiftUI 界面、采用 Liquid Glass 等现代 iOS 模式、审查运行时性能，并通过由 XcodeBuildMCP 驱动的工作流在模拟器中调试应用。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>界面框架</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI（需联网）</a></td> <td>在保持界面代码清晰易读的同时，可快速为 iPhone 和 iPad 原型化视图、导航和共享状态。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>构建工具</td> <td>xcodebuild 或 <a href=\"https://docs.tuist.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tuist（需联网）</a></td> <td>两者都能让原生构建循环留在终端中，而不依赖 Xcode 图形界面。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>项目自动化</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP（需联网）</a></td> <td>当你需要 Codex 检查 scheme 和 target、启动应用、截取屏幕截图，并在代理循环中持续迭代时，这是很好的选择。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>分发工具</td> <td><a href=\"https://asccli.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Store Connect CLI（需联网）</a></td> <td>让代理始终参与流程，并可直接将应用构建产物提交到 App Store。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>搭建应用和构建循环</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">搭建一个基础 SwiftUI 应用，并添加一个构建与启动脚本，方便我在本地环境中将它连接到 `Build` 操作。\n\n约束：\n- 以命令行为先。优先使用 Apple 的 `xcodebuild`；如果采用更简洁的设置有帮助，也可以使用 Tuist。\n- 如果代码库已经有完整 Xcode 项目，就使用 XcodeBuildMCP 列出 targets，选择正确的 scheme，进行构建、启动，并在迭代过程中截取屏幕截图。\n- 如果代码库已有模型、导航模式和共享工具，就复用它们。\n- 除非我明确要求共享 Apple 平台实现，否则只聚焦 iPhone 和 iPad。\n- 每次改动后采用小而可信的验证循环；只有较窄范围的检查通过后，才扩大到更广的构建。\n- 告诉我这是从零搭建，还是改动了现有项目。\n\n交付：\n- 应用基础框架或我要求的功能片段\n- 小型构建与启动脚本及其确切命令\n- 你实际运行的最小相关验证步骤\n- 使用的准确 scheme、模拟器和检查项\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"scaffold-the-app-and-build-loop\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">搭建应用和构建循环</h2> <p>对于从零开始的项目，先用普通提示词即可。让 Codex 搭建一个基础 iOS SwiftUI 应用，并写一个小型构建与启动脚本，方便你将它连接到<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/local-environment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地环境（本地尚未收录）</a>中的 <code>Build</code> 操作。</p> <p>保持命令行为先。Apple 的 <code>xcodebuild</code> 能从终端列出 scheme，并执行构建、测试、归档、<code>build-for-testing</code> 和 <code>test-without-building</code> 操作；这样 Codex 可以保持代理式循环，而不必来回切换到 Xcode 图形界面。</p> <p>如果你想使用更整洁的项目生成器，也愿意采用第三方工具，可以进一步了解 <a href=\"https://tuist.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tuist（需联网）</a>。它能在不打开图形界面的情况下生成并构建 Xcode 项目，Codex 仍可从终端构建并启动应用。</p> <p>进入完整 Xcode 项目后，如果需要更深入的自动化，可以使用 <a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP（需联网）</a>。当你需要处理 scheme、target、模拟器控制、截图、日志和界面交互，而普通 shell 命令已无法覆盖全部需求时，就该使用它。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用技能</h2> <p>第一轮通常不需要技能或 MCP 服务器。等工作变得专业化，或你希望把更强的 SwiftUI 惯例融入运行流程时，再添加技能。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/AvdLee/SwiftUI-Agent-Skill\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI expert（需联网）</a> 是一个通用的 SwiftUI 技能，已经涵盖许多最佳实践。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/twostraws/SwiftUI-Agent-Skill/blob/main/swiftui-pro/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI Pro（需联网）</a> 是覆盖面较广的 SwiftUI 审查技能，侧重现代 API、可维护性、辅助功能和性能。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-liquid-glass/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Liquid Glass expert（需联网）</a> 可帮助 Codex 使用新的 iOS 26 Liquid Glass API，并调整自定义组件，使其符合最新系统设计。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-performance-audit/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI performance（需联网）</a> 适用于功能变慢或 SwiftUI 视图更新路径可疑的情况；它会扫描常见问题，并按优先级报告应修复之处和最值得关注的性能瓶颈。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swift-concurrency-expert/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swift concurrency expert（需联网）</a> 适用于难以理解的错误或编译器警告阻碍你完成改动的情况。使用 GPT-5.6 Terra 时，可能较少需要此技能；不过 Swift 并发诊断变得嘈杂时，它依然有帮助。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-view-refactor/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI view refactor（需联网）</a> 有助于缩小文件并让 SwiftUI 代码保持一致。</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-ui-patterns/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI patterns（需联网）</a> 有助于随着代码库变大，采用可预测的 <code>@Observable</code> 和 <code>@Environment</code> 架构模式。</li> </ul> <p>如需了解如何安装和使用技能，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能文档（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"iterate\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">迭代</h2> <p>第一版可以运行后，或者你从现有项目开始时，就可以继续迭代界面或行为。</p> <p>描述清楚要改什么以及打算如何改，会有助于 Codex 更准确地完成这部分工作。</p> <p>把提示词中的背景条件说清楚：告诉 Codex 它是在从零搭建代码库，还是在修改现有 Xcode 项目；哪些 iOS 设备或部署目标必须继续支持；以及你希望它采用怎样的验证循环。</p> <p><a id=\"example-prompt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">示例提示词</h3> <p>例如，如果要为现有应用添加功能，可以这样提出要求：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add the onboarding flow for this SwiftUI app.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Reuse existing models, navigation patterns, and shared utilities.\n- Use XcodeBuildMCP to list the right targets or schemes, build the app, launch it, and capture screenshots if you need visual verification.\n- Keep the implementation focused on iPhone and iPad unless I explicitly ask for a shared iOS/macOS abstraction.\n- Tell me exactly which scheme, simulator, and checks you used.\n\nImplement the slice, verify it with the smallest relevant build or run loop, and summarize what changed.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">为这个 SwiftUI 应用添加新用户引导流程。\n\n约束：\n\n- 复用现有模型、导航模式和共享工具。\n- 使用 XcodeBuildMCP 列出正确的 target 或 scheme，构建并启动应用；如需视觉验证，截取屏幕截图。\n- 除非我明确要求共享的 iOS/macOS 抽象层，否则实现只聚焦 iPhone 和 iPad。\n- 准确告诉我使用了哪个 scheme、模拟器以及哪些检查。\n\n实现这部分功能，用最小的相关构建或运行循环进行验证，并总结改动。</div></div> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">实用建议</h2> <p><a id=\"start-with-basics\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">从基础开始</h3> <p>对于从零开始的项目，先用普通提示词即可。让 Codex 搭建一个基础应用，并编写小型构建与启动脚本，方便你将它连接到<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/local-environment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地环境（本地尚未收录）</a>中的 <code>Build</code> 操作。第一轮通常不需要技能或 MCP 服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"use-a-small-trustworthy-validation-loop\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">使用可信的小型验证循环</h3> <p>每次改动后，让 Codex 运行能够证明相关约定的最小命令。等后续需要时再扩大到更全面的构建。这样可以保持 Codex 高效，同时不必假装每次编辑都需要构建整个应用。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-the-loop-cli-first\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">保持命令行为先的构建流程</h3> <p>让构建流程以命令行为先。Apple 的 <code>xcodebuild</code> 工具可以列出 scheme，并执行构建、测试、归档、<code>build-for-testing</code> 和 <code>test-without-building</code> 操作，这样 Codex 就能持续处于代理循环中，而不必跳转到 Xcode 图形界面。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-xcodebuildmcp\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"xcode-xcodebuildmcp\">进入完整 Xcode 项目后使用 XcodeBuildMCP</h3> <p>一旦进入完整 Xcode 项目，并需要更深入地自动化，就应使用 XcodeBuildMCP。此时已经需要检查 scheme 和 target、控制模拟器、截取屏幕截图、查看日志和操作界面，单靠 shell 命令已不足以覆盖完整流程。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-for-ios\">Build for iOS</h1> <p>Use Codex to scaffold, build, and debug SwiftUI apps for iPhone and iPad.</p> <p>Use Codex to scaffold iOS SwiftUI projects, keep the build loop CLI-first with <code>xcodebuild</code> or Tuist, and add XcodeBuildMCP or focused SwiftUI skills when the work gets deeper.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Greenfield iOS SwiftUI apps where you want Codex to scaffold the app and build loop from scratch</li> <li>Existing iPhone and iPad projects where Codex needs schemes, simulator output, screenshots, or UI automation before the work is done</li> <li>Teams that want long-running iOS UI tasks to stay agentic and CLI-first instead of depending on the Xcode GUI</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Build or refactor SwiftUI UI, adopt modern iOS patterns such as Liquid Glass, audit runtime performance, and debug apps on simulators with XcodeBuildMCP-backed workflows.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>UI framework</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI (online)</a></td> <td>The fastest way to prototype views, navigation, and shared state for iPhone and iPad while keeping the UI code readable.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Build tooling</td> <td>xcodebuild or <a href=\"https://docs.tuist.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tuist (online)</a></td> <td>Both keep the native build loop in the terminal instead of depending on the Xcode GUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Project automation</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP (online)</a></td> <td>A strong option once you need Codex to inspect schemes and targets, launch the app, capture screenshots, and keep iterating without leaving the agentic loop.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Distribution tooling</td> <td><a href=\"https://asccli.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Store Connect CLI (online)</a></td> <td>Keep your agent fully in the loop and send your app build directly to the App Store.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Scaffold the App and Build Loop</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Scaffold a starter SwiftUI app and add a build-and-launch script I can wire to a `Build` action in my local environment.\n\nConstraints:\n- Stay CLI-first. Prefer Apple's `xcodebuild`; if a cleaner setup helps, it's okay to use Tuist.\n- If this repo already contains a full Xcode project, use XcodeBuildMCP to list targets, pick the right scheme, build, launch, and capture screenshots while you iterate.\n- Reuse existing models, navigation patterns, and shared utilities when they already exist.\n- Keep the app focused on iPhone and iPad unless I explicitly ask for a shared Apple-platform implementation.\n- Use a small trustworthy validation loop after each change, then expand to broader builds only when the narrower check passes.\n- Tell me whether you treated this as a greenfield scaffold or an existing-project change.\n\nDeliver:\n- the app scaffold or requested feature slice\n- a small build-and-launch script with the exact commands\n- the smallest relevant validation steps you ran\n- the exact scheme, simulator, and checks you used\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"scaffold-the-app-and-build-loop\">Scaffold the app and build loop</h2> <p>For greenfield work, start with plain prompting. Ask Codex to scaffold a starter iOS SwiftUI app and write a small build-and-launch script you can wire to a <code>Build</code> action in a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/local-environment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">local environment (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <p>Keep the loop CLI-first. Apple's <code>xcodebuild</code> can list schemes and handle build, test, archive, <code>build-for-testing</code>, and <code>test-without-building</code> actions from the terminal, which lets Codex stay in an agentic loop instead of bouncing into the Xcode GUI.</p> <p>If you want a cleaner project generator and you're comfortable with third-party tooling, <a href=\"https://tuist.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tuist (online)</a> is a good next step. It can generate and build Xcode projects without needing the GUI, while still letting Codex build and launch the app from the terminal.</p> <p>Use <a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP (online)</a> once you're inside a full Xcode project and need deeper automation. That's when schemes, targets, simulator control, screenshots, logs, and UI interaction matter enough that plain shell commands stop being the whole story.</p> <h2 id=\"leverage-skills\">Leverage skills</h2> <p>For the first pass, you often don't need a skill or MCP server. Add skills once the work gets specialized or you want stronger SwiftUI conventions baked into the run.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/AvdLee/SwiftUI-Agent-Skill\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI expert (online)</a> is a strong general-purpose SwiftUI skill with a lot of best practices already baked in.</li> <li> <p><a href=\"https://github.com/twostraws/SwiftUI-Agent-Skill/blob/main/swiftui-pro/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI Pro (online)</a> is a broad SwiftUI review skill for modern APIs, maintainability, accessibility, and performance.</p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-liquid-glass/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Liquid Glass expert (online)</a> helps Codex adopt the new iOS 26 Liquid Glass APIs and tune custom components so they fit the latest system design.</p> </li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-performance-audit/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI performance (online)</a> helps when a feature feels slow or a SwiftUI view update path looks suspicious. It scans for common SwiftUI mistakes and produces a prioritized report of what to fix and where the biggest gains are.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swift-concurrency-expert/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Swift concurrency expert (online)</a> helps when cryptic errors and compiler warnings start fighting the change you want to make. On GPT-5.6 Terra, you may need it less often, but it's still useful when Swift concurrency diagnostics get noisy.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-view-refactor/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI view refactor (online)</a> helps keep files smaller and make SwiftUI code more consistent across the repo.</li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/Dimillian/Skills/blob/main/swiftui-ui-patterns/SKILL.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI patterns (online)</a> helps reach for predictable <code>@Observable</code> and <code>@Environment</code> architecture patterns as the app grows.</li> </ul> <p>To learn more about how to install and use skills, see our <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skills documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"iterate\">Iterate</h2> <p>Once you have a first pass working, or if you're starting from an existing project, you can start iterating on the UI or behavior.</p> <p>For this part, be specific about what you want to change and how you want to change it.</p> <p>Make that prompting layer explicit: tell Codex whether it's working in a greenfield repo or an existing Xcode project, which iOS devices or deployment targets must keep working, and what validation loop you expect.</p> <h3 id=\"example-prompt\">Example prompt</h3> <p>For example, if you want to add a feature to an existing app, you can ask Codex for a change like this:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add the onboarding flow for this SwiftUI app.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Reuse existing models, navigation patterns, and shared utilities.\n- Use XcodeBuildMCP to list the right targets or schemes, build the app, launch it, and capture screenshots if you need visual verification.\n- Keep the implementation focused on iPhone and iPad unless I explicitly ask for a shared iOS/macOS abstraction.\n- Tell me exactly which scheme, simulator, and checks you used.\n\nImplement the slice, verify it with the smallest relevant build or run loop, and summarize what changed.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"start-with-basics\">Start with basics</h3> <p>Start with plain prompting for greenfield work. Ask Codex to scaffold a starter SwiftUI app and write a small build-and-launch script you can wire to a <code>Build</code> action in a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/environments/local-environment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">local environment (not in this local snapshot)</a>. For that first pass, you often don't need any skill or MCP server.</p> <h3 id=\"use-a-small-trustworthy-validation-loop\">Use a small trustworthy validation loop</h3> <p>After each change, tell Codex to run the narrowest command that actually proves the contract you touched. Expand to broader builds later. This keeps Codex fast without pretending a full app build is required for every edit.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-the-loop-cli-first\">Keep the loop CLI-first</h3> <p>Keep the loop CLI-first. Apple's <code>xcodebuild</code> tool can list schemes and run build, test, archive, <code>build-for-testing</code>, and <code>test-without-building</code> actions from the terminal, which lets Codex stay in an agentic loop instead of bouncing into the Xcode GUI.</p> <h3 id=\"leverage-xcodebuildmcp\">Leverage XcodeBuildMCP</h3> <p>Use XcodeBuildMCP as soon as you are inside a full Xcode project and need deeper automation. That's the point where schemes, targets, simulator control, screenshots, logs, and UI interaction matter enough that plain shell commands stop being the whole story.</p>"};
